  "body": "Fixes #2832. Design #3068 Phase 2 (parsed files in tools) for sync-models.\n\n## Problem\nA parseable-but-wrong-shaped `opencode.jsonc` (`\"google\": \"oops\"`, `\"models\": \"oops\"`, an array provider entry, or no `provider` key at all) crashed sync-models with raw TypeErrors naming neither the file nor the key — in `run()`'s provider derefs and in the JSONC tree editor's `members` walks — blocking sync for every provider until a human guessed the bad key.\n\n## Changes (bin/sync-models.mjs)\n- **`validateConfigShape(config, configPath)`** runs immediately after `parseJsonc` in `run()`, in the same clean-exit path as a parse error: root, `provider`, each provider entry, and each `models` container must be plain objects, otherwise one named error — `invalid config shape in <path>: provider.google: expected object, got string`. Whole-job refusal with a diagnostic, per the #3068 Phase 2 leaning recorded for #2832.\n- **Missing `provider` key = nothing to sync**, not a crash: the two remaining `config.provider` derefs (antigravity block, openai sync) now use optional chaining.\n- **Tree editor guards:** `setJsoncPath` / `removeJsoncPath` refuse a non-object intermediate node with an error naming the full key path and the offending prefix, instead of dereferencing `members` on a scalar/array node.\n\n## Tests (bin/sync-models.test.mjs)\nNew #2832 tests pin: scalar provider entry, array provider entry, scalar `models`, wrong-shaped `provider` container and root, missing `provider` key (no throw), well-formed config (no throw), tree-editor refusal for scalar/array intermediates, and the well-formed set control. Laptop run: `node --test bin/sync-models.test.mjs` — 35 pass, 0 fail (all pre-existing tests stay green). Oracle: the named-error messages above; before this change the same shapes threw `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'find')` / `Cannot create property … on string 'oops'`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793536&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7975&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7975&signature=49a4c9fb1ca885b435e1e2590c804e0c0a7043edc437b6b3d332c1f5a8ad9302\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7975?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
